{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans","id":1475758,"title":"Asian American Changeling type: Cathayans","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-03-03T18:49:46-08:00","id":1475758,"title":"Asian American Changeling type: Cathayans","content":"In an idea for a Changeling chronicle that focuses on Asian American Changelings, I describe that there are three types of Asian American changelings.<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>The Changelings and Courts of Asia who immigrated to the West, following their families or setting up powerbases in the West.</li> <li>Changelings who are of Asian descent but born in America.</li> </ol>And 3) Asians who were made sold into the service of Western Fae.<br /> <br /> I especially want to use the third group to explore the long historical, economic, and political connections the West has had with Asia. I think this type of Asian American or Asian European Changelings was especially common during the era of European Imperial Expansion, China\u2019s <i>century of national humiliation, </i>the mass immigration of Chinese and Japanese to the US during in the mid to late 1800\u2019s, and then the occupation of Japan after WW2.<br /> <br /> I refer to this third group as Cathayans, because I want to explore the bias, bigotry, and stereotyping Asians have had to confront.Yet I also wanted to emphasize that intolerance is not limited to white people. Unfortunately, the peoples of Asia can be hostile to each other and their own peoples.Certain countries would be hostile to Cathayans, especially the more traditional courts.<br /> <br /> For examples of how I envision playing Cathayan characters, here is a description of a Japanese Cathayan character and a general description of Japanese Cathayans in the US. Japanese Cathayans can be found in Brazil, Canada, Europe, and Mexico.<br /> <br /> Cathayan Characters<br /> <br /> <b><i>Madame Butterfly</i></b>(Kiku Saito) is a fairest nightsinger and the Spring Queen of Little Tokyo in San Fransisco. In 1883, She was originally a Geisha from Nagasaki, whose voice was so beautiful it drew her a long list of clients. So beautiful was her voice, that it caught the attention of an American sailor, who was also a changeling racketeer. He courted and pretended to want to marry her, but then sold her to Western True Fae, Lover with Crimson Roses. When she escaped, she found herself in San Francisco, California. It was the year 1920, World War 1 had just ended and the jazz age was about to go into full swing. She settled in San Francisco\u2019s Japan Town in the Western Audition and made a living for herself singing in a nightclub. As a Cathayan, she now spoke English better than her native language and quickly built a backstory for herself based on Giacomo Puccini\u2019s <b><i>Madame Butterfly </i></b>and was given that title. Her physical beauty her voice, and her ability to quickly adjust to the expectations of her white audience won her the admiration of many Western Changelings and mortals.<br /> <br /> For more than a decade, fear and resentment had been growing among white Americans of Asian Americans taking their jobs, the \u201c<i>yellow peril\u201d. </i>Even after the Immigration Act of 1924, attacks and excluding Asian Americans from Asian jobs continued. <b><i>Madame Butterfly </i></b>used her connections in the white police force and among white politicians to buy some protection for the Japanese Americans and Cathayans. When President Roosevelt signed Executive Order 9066, forcibly moving more than 120,000 Japanese Americans to internment camps, used her influence to provide the people in her camp with more goods and services than Japanese Americans in other internment camps enjoyed.<br /> <br /> After the war, <b><i>Madame Butterfly, </i></b>was one of the few Japanese American Cathayans to return to Japan Town in the Western Audition. While initially very, very small, during the US occupation of Japan, a new wave of Japanese Cathayans found their way to the Japan Town in the Western District. <b><i>Madame Butterfly </i></b>helped build the new freehold in Japan Town. Because of her political connections, she quickly became the Spring Monarch. When the courts of Japan began moving to San Francisco during the 1980s, <b><i>Madame Butterfly </i></b>built political ties with these courts and acted as a mediator between them Western Seasonal Courts, and the Cathayan Seasonal Courts.<br /> <br /> In modern nights <b><i>Madame Butterfly </i></b>is one of the most influential Changelings in San Francisco, having strong political ties between the different courts and freeholds in the city.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Appearance</i></b><br /> <br /> Despite having lived in San Francisco for more than a hundred years, she still looks like a young woman in her early twenties <i>(Note: I have given her a merit called ageless beauty, which negates the penalties of aging and using the mechanics that at wyrd 7 +150 years to the changeling\u2019s lifespan). </i>Her mask shows a tall, beautiful Japanese woman with jet black hair to her waste. Possessing the ideal of Japanese feminine beauty, her hair is jet black and her skin is very pale.<br /> Her mien looks how modern fantasy artists view of a sidhe from Asia. Behind the mask, her skin is porcelain white, her hair is a sky blue, and her huge, oblong eyes are a deep purple. She also possesses claws, large pointed, dog-like ears, and a tail.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T18:51:32-08:00","id":1475759,"title":"","content":"<b><i>Japanese Cathayans: </i></b>The first Japanese to fall into servitude of Western Fae might have started as far back as the 1540\u2019s, when the Portuguese first came to Japan. The records of the Fae of Portugal and Netherlands, indicate that there were at least 7 changelings of Japanese descent among their court, before Tokugawa Iemitsu closed the country to foreign influence in 1623. However, it did not become common until the Meiji Period, after Commodore Perry\u2019s black ships forcibly opened the country. In Japan the stability and strength of Japan\u2019s courts kept the racketeers of the West from dragging hundreds of their people into slavery as compared to the courts of China and other Asian countries, which had been made into Western colonies, Western racketeers WERE able to net many of its people into the hands of their Gentry. Many more fell into nets, immigrating to Hawaii and then mainland USA. The number of Japanese falling into Western hands began to slow after Theodore Roosevelt\u2019s <b>Gentlemen's Agreement of 1907.</b> Japan agrees to not allow more immigration from Japan to the US and the US agreed to not impose restrictions on Japanese immigrants already in the US. Immigration comes to a halt after the Immigration act of 1924. The Japanese Cathayan community stops growing, begins to shrink, and is then scattered when Japanese Americans are put in internment camps.<br /> <br /> The Japanese Cathayan community started to regrow during the US occupation of Japan. Because the Japanese Imperial Changeling Courts were smashed at the end of World War 2, they are incapable to stopping US racketeers from dragging Japanese men, women (especially Geisha) and children into slavery for the Western Gentry. It would not be until the mid-70\u2019s the Japanese courts would be strong to bring this to a halt. Many more Japanese fell into traps from US loyalists, traveling to study at US universities and do business in the United States.<br /> In modern nights, large communities can be found in California, Hawaii, Illinois, New York, Ohio, and Washington. Though Japanese Cathayans can be found in unexpected places like Alaska, Alabama, Florida, Georgia, and Virginia.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Appearance</i></b><br /> <br /> Japanese Cathayans are distinct from other changelings from Japan in that their Western Keepers gave them features associated with Westerners like blonde or red hair and blue or green eyes. Some have skin that is as dark as an African American or a Hispanics. High wyrd Japanese Cathayans looks like Japanese versions of Western Fae. It is usually clear to tell which Japanese were spirited away prior to the late 1970\u2019s from those spirited away after 1980. Because of the popularity of manga and anime, their Western Keepers give them eye and hair color like blood red, cotton candy pink, green, purple, and sky blue. Western Keepers like to give their Cathayans a fusion of Western and Asian beauty. Japanese women taken after 1980 have slender forms, but large firm breasts that are too big and too perfect to not be REALLY good plastic surgery or the gift of the gods.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Demographics</i></b><br /> <br /> The Japanese Cathayan community is shockingly large compared to the mortal Japanese American community. This is largely because of two factors; 1) While many Japanese Cathayans have lived in the US for decades or more than a century, they have never officially become US citizens 2) Many Cathayans use the power of the wyrd to live beyond the mortal lifespan and remove the effects of aging.<br /> <br /> While it DOES still happen, the number of Japanese being spirited away by Westerners has dwindled to a small handful. This is due to a combination of the number of Japanese traveling to the US for business and education has shrunk to a small fraction of the height during the 1990s. Also, the graying of Japan\u2019s population means fewer are immigrating to other countries. The extended lifespan the wyrd prevents the Japanese Cathayan population from shrinking the way the mortal Japanese American community is.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Court System: </i></b>The Japanese Cathayans in the United States use the Seasonal Court system, BUT one that uses themes and concepts from Japanese belief system.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Relationship with Western Courts: </i></b>Like their mortal counterparts, Japanese Cathayans have confronted bias and bigotry through much of their early history in the United States. After 1960\u2019s, this lessened a great deal. HOWEVER, after the arrival of covid and Donald Trump blamed China for its spread in the US, they have been confronting attacks by White changelings and mortals. Western loyalists and racketeers are especially fanning these flames.<br /> <br /> <b><i>Relationship with Japanese Courts: </i></b>While the Japanese Courts do not feel the same hostility, suspicion and contempt, the other Asian courts feel for their Cathayan counterparts, they do not regard them as truly Japanese. This a result of Cathayans having Western features and mannerisms. They are treated as a US court distinct from the other Western Courts.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T19:32:50-08:00","id":1475760,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans#post1475758\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I refer to this third group as Cathayans, because I want to explore the bias, bigotry, and stereotyping Asians have had to confront.Yet I also wanted to emphasize that intolerance is not limited to white people. Unfortunately, the peoples of Asia can be hostile to each other and their own peoples.Certain countries would be hostile to Cathayans, especially the more traditional courts.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, please, do not use the word &quot;Cathayans&quot; here. This is an archaic word used during a period when Europeans knew little about what was going on in central and eastern Asia, derived from the Khitan of northern China and misattributed to other territories of China. Referring to people from Japan or Korea as Cathayans is like referring to Peru as &quot;the East Indies&quot; or to the Spanish and the Irish as &quot;vikings.&quot; Korea in particular has a history of resisting foreign invasions, including by the Khitan specifically. It is kind of rude to call them Chinese people.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yeah, I understand what you guys mean, sorry<img src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/> One themes I wanted to touch upon with the characters was Western biases and racism towards peoples of Asia. I chose the term Cathayan, because it was the term the Kindred <i>(Vampire: The Masquerade)</i> used for the Kue-jin from <i>Kindred of the East.</i> I should have done more research on the term.</div> </div> </div> </div>So I guess we're just doing this again and old feedback hasn't been listened to, back to using the Kindred of the East word that means &quot;Chinese,&quot; which leads you to refer to Japanese victims of faerie human trafficking as Japanese Chinese People. Back to this weird focus on ethnic physical features and racial transformation. The signature character is literally Madame Butterfly.<br /> <br /> The material you've written on this subject, however well intentioned, has a pretty bad problem with othering. I feel obliged at least to post this so as not to leave it unchallenged, but I don't feel listened to after the last thread, so saying anything more feels pointless.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T21:22:10-08:00","id":1475764,"title":"","content":"Okay, so having just realized that this is an obsession that has been going on a while and has roots, I need to step back and ground myself on this, so I have some questions.<br /> <br /> 1) Yikes.<br /> <br /> Sorry, not a question, but for all the reasons Loserman has mentioned, it needs to be said, yikes.<br /> <br /> 2) Is this for an actual game that's going to be played/is playing/was played but still can't get out of your head, or is this all a hypothetical?<br /> <br /> 3) Why is the theme of &quot;the bias, bigotry, and stereotyping Asians have had to confront&quot; a theme you want to particularly explore in a gaming scenario, and...<br /> <br /> 4) ...why Changeling in particular for it, as opposed to, say, Deviant, Beast, or Promethean?<br /> <br /> 5) Why, in exploration of this idea, is it pertinent to have a particular delineation between the types of Lost you're talking about in the first place? Changeling tends to have lean towards the trauma of Arcadia being more of a unifying subject than something that retains the earthly politics that changelings are snatched from or return to, and in the cases where divisions between freeholds come in, like in Victorian Lost, a lot of those factors relate those back to issues of the Fae itself, or in ways in which the Durance bleeds back into connecting back into human society.<br /> <br /> Like, yes, Asian American changelings are going to have to deal with the fact that white America has a lot of obstacles that makes being one of the Lost even harder, and that Asian communities are going to a) carry over prejudices from their own home countries, and b) are going to have their own metrics of what constitutes a betrayal of roots, but I have trouble of relating that to how Lost Society is going to fracture around and along those same lines into the same granular things when all changelings basically experience trauma at the hands of eldritch abominations who are just as clearly disconnected from the stories they appropriate for form as they crudely follow them without a particularly compelling reason for that to happen.( There are no &quot;'Western' Fae&quot;, there are &quot;Fairies who predate and exploit from 'Western' locations.&quot; Faerie has no west, let alone a Europe.)<br /> <br /> 6) There's also something very confusing about the whataboutism in play in trying to tackle this. Yes. Asian communites had their own struggles and strife with each other that would make creating a cohseive block problematic for decades on end, but much like how I have to ask &quot;What does all this granulation have to do with the protection against the True Fae?&quot;, fixating on how that happened feels like it's focusing on molehills versus the mountain of a problem that was American politics against immigrants and immigration. For some pure historical research, that could be interesting to learn and wrap into future planning for, but for a game's purposes, you already have a game that is setup between the tyranny of two major forces (An America in which you are not white, and the True Fae), getting into schisms on Asian American Communities while trying to rationalize that within the context of the fairies feels like it wouldn't be particularly fun as a whole focus (maybe a factor for a character's story it'd work?), and feels like some kind of safe cultural fetish-wanting to get into the plight of Asian Americans while trying to make white players feel okay about it because &quot;They did it to themselves, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly, this entire thing feels squicky to me, and I'm hoping that the answers to these questions does something to resolve that going forward.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-04-2022, 12:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-03T21:36:51-08:00","id":1475765,"title":"","content":"...ok I'm Japanese-Chinese American and just...no. Way too much exotizing here for it to be viable, and in the worse case leans into the worst parts of WoD splat design of tying cultures to splats.<br /> <br /> To be honest, all of this sounds more like belonging to Changeling: the Dreaming and not Lost in tying fae to specific cultures, which is something Lost specifically tried to steer away from. So why Lost?<br /> <br /> (and I'm speaking as someone who finds Dreaming to be their favorite WoD gameline, but even I'm cognizant if its many many Problems)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4418,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","user":"tasti man LH","date":". 03-04-2022, 02:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":9}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4418-tasti-man-lh","name":"tasti man LH","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4418_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1850"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T13:19:47-08:00","id":1475796,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475764#post1475764\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, so having just realized that this is an obsession that has been going on a while and has roots, I need to step back and ground myself on this, so I have some questions.<br /> <br /> 1) Yikes.<br /> <br /> Sorry, not a question, but for all the reasons Loserman has mentioned, it needs to be said, yikes.<br /> <br /> 2) Is this for an actual game that's going to be played/is playing/was played but still can't get out of your head, or is this all a hypothetical?<br /> <br /> 3) Why is the theme of &quot;the bias, bigotry, and stereotyping Asians have had to confront&quot; a theme you want to particularly explore in a gaming scenario, and...<br /> <br /> 4) ...why Changeling in particular for it, as opposed to, say, Deviant, Beast, or Promethean?<br /> <br /> 5) Why, in exploration of this idea, is it pertinent to have a particular delineation between the types of Lost you're talking about in the first place? Changeling tends to have lean towards the trauma of Arcadia being more of a unifying subject than something that retains the earthly politics that changelings are snatched from or return to, and in the cases where divisions between freeholds come in, like in Victorian Lost, a lot of those factors relate those back to issues of the Fae itself, or in ways in which the Durance bleeds back into connecting back into human society.<br /> <br /> Like, yes, Asian American changelings are going to have to deal with the fact that white America has a lot of obstacles that makes being one of the Lost even harder, and that Asian communities are going to a) carry over prejudices from their own home countries, and b) are going to have their own metrics of what constitutes a betrayal of roots, but I have trouble of relating that to how Lost Society is going to fracture around and along those same lines into the same granular things when all changelings basically experience trauma at the hands of eldritch abominations who are just as clearly disconnected from the stories they appropriate for form as they crudely follow them without a particularly compelling reason for that to happen.( There are no &quot;'Western' Fae&quot;, there are &quot;Fairies who predate and exploit from 'Western' locations.&quot; Faerie has no west, let alone a Europe.)<br /> <br /> 6) There's also something very confusing about the whataboutism in play in trying to tackle this. Yes. Asian communites had their own struggles and strife with each other that would make creating a cohseive block problematic for decades on end, but much like how I have to ask &quot;What does all this granulation have to do with the protection against the True Fae?&quot;, fixating on how that happened feels like it's focusing on molehills versus the mountain of a problem that was American politics against immigrants and immigration. For some pure historical research, that could be interesting to learn and wrap into future planning for, but for a game's purposes, you already have a game that is setup between the tyranny of two major forces (An America in which you are not white, and the True Fae), getting into schisms on Asian American Communities while trying to rationalize that within the context of the fairies feels like it wouldn't be particularly fun as a whole focus (maybe a factor for a character's story it'd work?), and feels like some kind of safe cultural fetish-wanting to get into the plight of Asian Americans while trying to make white players feel okay about it because &quot;They did it to themselves, too.&quot;<br /> <br /> Honestly, this entire thing feels squicky to me, and I'm hoping that the answers to these questions does something to resolve that going forward.</div> </div> </div> </div>1&amp;2) I am developing a chronicle which includes changelings from the Little Tokyo freehold.<br /> <br /> While I referred them as Cathayans when developing the three types of Asian Americans, the characters and players do not call them such.<br /> <br /> Kiku Saito took the title <b><i>Madame Butterfly</i></b> to play on white stereotypes and the popularity of the play to buy political connections.<br /> <br /> 3) I don't focus on it, but it is in the background. I wrote a general history of the groups to explain why certain characters act the way they do.<br /> <br /> 4). Because I am a huge fan of fae folklore and mythology, plus <b><i>Changeling: The Lost</i></b> is my favorite game from Chronicles of Darkness<br /> <br /> 5 and 6) I would argue that trauma can heighten instead of lessoning cultural, national, and political identities, as we have seen in contemporary politics. I do see the different factions working together to deal with threats from the True Fae and attacks against the Asian community, but it wouldn't remove their cultural and political identities. The Asian American changelings do not officially break themselves into three types, but there is bias against the Asian changelings of the seasonal courts. I did not mean this to be whataboutism. I drew it from my courses on China and Japanese culture and history at Emory University and Georgia Tech. Plus, some experiences some of my Chinese American friends have had in China.<br /> <br /> When I said Western Fae, I meant the fae creatures and monsters of folklore from Western Europe and North America.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T14:48:20-08:00","id":1475800,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475796#post1475796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">While I referred them as Cathayans when developing the three types of Asian Americans, the characters and players do not call them such.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do <i>you</i> call them such? What is one good reason to use this word to refer to this concept? Kindred of the East did not invent this word. It has a real life meaning referring to people from a region of northern China.<br /> <br /> I see a lot of influence from Kindred of the East on this. The factionalism focused around cultural origin, the exoticization, the anachronisms that leave modern characters feeling trapped in generations-old history, the immortality which is not a common trait in Changeling: the Lost, and of course, the conspicuous word &quot;Cathayan.&quot; I don't think these influences do your material any good.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475796#post1475796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Kiku Saito took the title <b><i>Madame Butterfly</i></b> to play on white stereotypes and the popularity of the play to buy political connections.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why did you also give her the background of the opera character as a geisha wooed and spurned by an American sailor?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":522,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","user":"Stupid Loserman","date":". 03-04-2022, 05:50 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T16:04:49-08:00","id":1475807,"title":"","content":"Speaking of KotE\u2026<br /> <br /> Madhatter, you may want to take a look at what hsienfan did with the Hungry Dead ie. Wan Kuei as Storyteller\u2019s Vault material. The links can be found on these forums and RPG.net\u2019s. The latter especially has multiple threads of \u2018open development\u2019 where you can see a lot of materials. (And I think the STV materials themselves were free; though I haven\u2019t downloaded them myself yet, and I don\u2019t know enough on how STV works to be sure) The Hungry Dead there play into the Asia-centric cultural and mythological motifs <b>without</b> relying on stereotypes as shorthands. I\u2019ve been reading and rereading the threads for days now, and it\u2019s good.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T17:29:19-08:00","id":1475814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Stupid Loserman</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475800#post1475800\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why do <i>you</i> call them such? What is one good reason to use this word to refer to this concept? Kindred of the East did not invent this word. It has a real life meaning referring to people from a region of northern China.<br /> <br /> I see a lot of influence from Kindred of the East on this. The factionalism focused around cultural origin, the exoticization, the anachronisms that leave modern characters feeling trapped in generations-old history, the immortality which is not a common trait in Changeling: the Lost, and of course, the conspicuous word &quot;Cathayan.&quot; I don't think these influences do your material any good.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> Why did you also give her the background of the opera character as a geisha wooed and spurned by an American sailor?</div> </div> </div> </div>As one of the earliest Asian American Changelings, I felt that than they confronted the most bigotry and ignorance of the three groups of Asian American Changelings. I felt oriental and yellow were far more offensive and chose Cathayan as the lesser of the three evils.<br /> <br /> I plead guilty to drawing inspiration from the old Kindred of the East Game, but another source of inspiration was the factionalism we are seeing here in the US. I also drew inspiration from my dads experience working in China and several courses I took on Chinese and Japanese culture.<br /> <br /> The mechanics I am using to explain the longevity of Changelings is beginning at Wyrd 7, the characters lifespan extends;<br /> wyrd 7 +150 years<br /> Wyrd 8 +300 years<br /> Wyrd 9 + 600 years<br /> Wyrd 10 the Changeling is more a being of dreams than of flesh and blood and no longer suffers penalties due to aging, disease, or drugs. With the exception of their frailties and cold iron, the Changeling only takes damage from supernatural attacks, which includes the based powers of changelings.<br /> <br /> I think there should be several ways to gain immortality, so some changelings can make a contract with death to no longer suffer penalties due to aging.<br /> <br /> The reason I used the background of a geisha wooed by an American sailor is that the play is based off of an autobiographical short story. I decided that this was a common tactic for Western racketeers to kidnap Japanese women.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-04T21:55:11-08:00","id":1475822,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475796#post1475796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> While I referred them as Cathayans when developing the three types of Asian Americans, the characters and players do not call them such.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Okay, I find that, as someone trying to go to bed, this is what I want to comment on:<br /> <br /> If neither character or player is going to call them such, <i>don't name them that</i>. Name them in such a way that people are going to <i>actually</i> use them.<br /> <br /> I don't think at this point it's any secret that your leaning into this is the major point of contention, but it's game designer 101 that your language needs to be as clear and direct as possible, and more importantly, readers will use whatever language you put down regardless of your intent, and many will justify continued usage of the language based on your deliberate usage.<br /> <br /> Everyone else has covered a lot of direct details, so listen to them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T10:50:44-08:00","id":1475847,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475822#post1475822\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Okay, I find that, as someone trying to go to bed, this is what I want to comment on:<br /> <br /> If neither character or player is going to call them such, <i>don't name them that</i>. Name them in such a way that people are going to <i>actually</i> use them.<br /> <br /> I don't think at this point it's any secret that your leaning into this is the major point of contention, but it's game designer 101 that your language needs to be as clear and direct as possible, and more importantly, readers will use whatever language you put down regardless of your intent, and many will justify continued usage of the language based on your deliberate usage.<br /> <br /> Everyone else has covered a lot of direct details, so listen to them.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The reason I am giving this type of Asian American Changeling so much emphasis is that I asked myself questions like;<ol class=\"decimal\"><li>After their escape why didn\u2019t they return to their homeland? As the former slaves of Western Gentry, I would assume they would be EXTREMLY eager to return to their native country.</li> <li>Why don\u2019t they join the Changelings courts of Asia?</li> </ol><br /> During their durance, they were forced to learn western languages like English, French, and German.They also developed Western mannerisms.As a result, many speak these languages and act more like the people of these countries.Their Keeper\u2019s also gave them features found in Westerners.So Changelings of their native courts not only accused them of being loyalists and racketeers, but also stooges of Western Imperial powers and drove them away.<br /> <br /> Also, while some Asian courts, like the Japanese Imperial Courts during the Meiji period, often traveled to the West to learn of the magics, technologies, even political system, most did not stay long to build bases on power.This did not really become popular until globalization started in the 1970\u2019s. As a result, the Asian American/Asian European Changelings developed a variation of Western courts, like the seasonal court system but drawing on themes from their countries.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T12:04:10-08:00","id":1475849,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475847#post1475847\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The reason I am giving this type of Asian American Changeling so much emphasis is</div> </div> </div> </div>No. Stop. This has nothing to do with the commentary.<br /> <br /> THe word you are using is problematic-hell, let's call it what it is, it's a racist term. You have been told as much long before now. You have admitted you don't intend for it to be used by characters, or players, which means it's a useless word to continue using in the design of it.<br /> <br /> We can talk later about all the other elements at play, but in regards to addressing the point I made in the previous point, <i>it's time to find another name</i>.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T15:32:19-08:00","id":1475859,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475849#post1475849\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> No. Stop. This has nothing to do with the commentary.<br /> <br /> THe word you are using is problematic-hell, let's call it what it is, it's a racist term. You have been told as much long before now. You have admitted you don't intend for it to be used by characters, or players, which means it's a useless word to continue using in the design of it.<br /> <br /> We can talk later about all the other elements at play, but in regards to addressing the point I made in the previous point, <i>it's time to find another name</i>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Alright, does anyone have any suggestions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T19:08:19-08:00","id":1475868,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475859#post1475859\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Alright, does anyone have any suggestions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Have you considered\u2026 <i>not?</i><br /> <br /> Like, this isn't a metaphysical concept we're talking about here, there doesn't have to be a <i>systematized extradiegetic term</i> for changelings whose durances for some reason gave them different racialized features than the ones they grew up with. Individual communities at odds with each other will likely have their own unpleasant names for the people down the way, and if you absolutely need a word for the general phenomenon it doesn't have to (and probably shouldn't) be specifically &quot;Asian&quot; changelings with &quot;Western&quot; features instead of [changeling's original culture] [concept name].<br /> <br /> &quot;Alienated&quot; is sufficiently niche in its existing use in Mage (and it's been established that this franchise doesn't worry too much about different gamelines using the same terms for different things) that I don't imagine you'd run into much issue using it for changeling's spatial equivalent to Lost returning to a time substantially different from their era of departure, but again, I'm not really convinced this is a thing that needs an enshrined capital-n Name for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T19:55:08-08:00","id":1475872,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475868#post1475868\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you considered\u2026 <i>not?</i><br /> <br /> Like, this isn't a metaphysical concept we're talking about here, there doesn't have to be a <i>systematized extradiegetic term</i> for changelings whose durances for some reason gave them different racialized features than the ones they grew up with. Individual communities at odds with each other will likely have their own unpleasant names for the people down the way, and if you absolutely need a word for the general phenomenon it doesn't have to (and probably shouldn't) be specifically &quot;Asian&quot; changelings with &quot;Western&quot; features instead of [changeling's original culture] [concept name].<br /> <br /> &quot;Alienated&quot; is sufficiently niche in its existing use in Mage (and it's been established that this franchise doesn't worry too much about different gamelines using the same terms for different things) that I don't imagine you'd run into much issue using it for changeling's spatial equivalent to Lost returning to a time substantially different from their era of departure, but again, I'm not really convinced this is a thing that needs an enshrined capital-n Name for it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I would argue alienation is a part of all of the games to various degrees and I want to use this type of Asian American/Asian European Changeling to talk about the long historical connections between the West and East, even its darkest parts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11066-madhatter","name":"Madhatter","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11066_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"746"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T21:12:41-08:00","id":1475876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475872#post1475872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I would argue alienation is a part of all of the games to various degrees</div> </div> </div> </div>You will get no argument from me there, but at least you wouldn't be <i>using a specific racist term</i> as the name a phenomenon that doesn't have any reason to be culturally-specific in its metaphysics.<br /> <br /> Changeling's always had &quot;you spent such a long and/or difficult time adjusting to life in another world that when you came back you couldn't relate to the people you grew up with&quot; in its metaphorical space, most directly by analogy to soldiers returning from war. If you're going to insist on spotlighting a particular artificial alienation by giving it a name relating to its cultural context, it should probably, y'know, <i>actually relate to the cultural context</i> instead of being the equivalent of calling all of these Asian changelings &quot;Chinaman.&quot;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and I want to use this type of Asian American/Asian European Changeling to talk about the long historical connections between the West and East, even its darkest parts. </div> </div> </div>Uh-huh.<br /> <br /> You can do that and still avoid giving the impression you <i>just want to engage in cultural fetishism</i> if you either don't try to give this narrow phenomenon a name in the system itself at all or if you name it for the general phenomenon so that you can discuss the particular instances of that phenomenon interacting with cultures you're interested in exploring.<br /> <br /> I can guarantee you, at least, that different Asian cultures are not going to have the same name for this phenomenon due to the simple linguistic fact of <i>those cultures don't speak the same primary language</i>. The only way that's happening is through a shared loanword coming from somewhere else, which rather fails to avoid the &quot;using a foreigner's faulty name for the people instead of the people's name for themselves&quot; problem, or by using a descriptive name that fits the common points between the names those cultures would use themselves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T21:53:08-08:00","id":1475877,"title":"","content":"Gonna agree with the other posters; this does not feel like a Good Way To Proceed. I recommend discarding this idea as well-intentioned-but-flawed.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1168-hobbitguy1420","name":"HobbitGuy1420","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1168_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"332"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-05T23:36:30-08:00","id":1475881,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475796#post1475796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">5 and 6) I would argue that trauma can heighten instead of lessoning cultural, national, and political identities, as we have seen in contemporary politics.</div> </div> </div> </div>I\u2019m not exactly a psychologist, and I even have extreme difficulties understanding other humans, but wouldn\u2019t the effects of trauma on strengthening or weakening bonds differ based on the cause and who receives them? I\u2019m pretty sure most Changeling don\u2019t suffer a durance that relates at all to cultural, national or even political identities. Being forced to be a sing forever, or be a stuffed toy doesn\u2019t exactly speak to me about reinforcing my national or cultural pride. (Not that I have much of either, but my point stands.) Even if it does strengthen certain bonds, I\u2019d argue that most Changelings would cling to things more tangible and less abstract than nation or ideology, like the ashes of their old home, or their significant other or even their fetch as things that represent who they once were. Plus there is the havoc seemings and kiths would have on things. I mean, I\u2019d say it\u2019s more likely that Changelings would have more loyalty to their motley, court, kith or seeming than they ever had for their old political or cultural identity unless that identity was absolutely core to who they were, or something that they thought they were. As for outside discrimination and such\u2026how would people even tell? I mean, when you look like a living bonfire or a humanoid lizard, how would anyone know whether you were from Georgia or Barcelona? And if I remember rightly, the mask doesn\u2019t have to reflect who you were. Depending on how the tell of something like being a little green wizened, or rainbow skin, or a spider manifests, people could mistake you for something completely different from what you once were.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475796#post1475796\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">but it wouldn't remove their cultural and political identities.</div> </div> </div> </div> I mean, I guess? I don\u2019t know, I\u2019m pretty sure if I spent a so long as a statue or a mirror or a flower that I forgot I was human, and knew I was potentially being hunted, I\u2019d be pretty unconcerned about human politics outside of immediate problems it might cause me or my motley. And culture\u2026 I think I would try an bury my self in wherever I ended up so I don\u2019t look suspicious when the huntsmen come around. As for identity as a whole, well\u2026that\u2019s what you lose when you become a Changeling. The thorns just tears so much away, and not everything makes it back to the fetch, or can be reclaimed even if it does. You won\u2019t ever be the same person you were.<br /> <br /> Also this entire concept feels very off putting to me. I think others have expressed similar sentiments. Maybe something to consider?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>To whomever reads this, I hope you have a good day/night. May you be Happy.<br /> <br /> So, I made some Mage Legacies <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1497183-templebuilder-s-new-legacy-thread#post1497183\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>, with some help. They vary in quality, but I hope you take a look at them. Every one contains pieces of me, for better or worse.","edited":{"userid":26736,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","user":"TempleBuilder","date":". 03-06-2022, 02:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26736-templebuilder","name":"TempleBuilder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26736_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1251"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T07:56:26-08:00","id":1475896,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Madhatter</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475872#post1475872\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I want to use this type of Asian American/Asian European Changeling to talk about the long historical connections between the West and East, even its darkest parts.</div> </div> </div> </div>You don't need it to do this. It doesn't help you do this. In fact, it's kind of fucked up and <i>itself represents</i> some of those darker parts.<br /> <br /> You're speaking very lightly about this issue. If I were trying to talk seriously about the Asian-American experience and how difficult and complicated their relationship is with racism and the preexisting conflicts between the different countries and regions of East Asia, and somebody told me the words I was using to tackle this issue were themselves racist and glossed over and conflated those different countries and regions, I would not shrug and say, &quot;what would be a better word to use then?&quot; I would be like &quot;wait, really? Shit, I'm sorry. Wow. I guess I missed something important there.&quot;<br /> <br /> As long as this is your attitude, you shouldn't be tackling this subject. You're making many more errors here that make this material clumsy at best and stereotypical and dismissive at worse, you're not aware of these errors, and you show no interest in finding and correcting them. It's that last quality that is the worst here, where the problem becomes willful.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/522-stupid-loserman","name":"Stupid Loserman","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar522_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1824"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T08:02:56-08:00","id":1475897,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TempleBuilder</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/1475758-asian-american-changeling-type-cathayans?p=1475881#post1475881\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And if I remember rightly, the mask doesn\u2019t have to reflect who you were. Depending on how the tell of something like being a little green wizened, or rainbow skin, or a spider manifests, people could mistake you for something completely different from what you once were.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per 1e: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Rites of Spring, p67</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>The Mask Is Recognizable:</b> With certain very rare exceptions, a changeling\u2019s Mask still looks as that changeling did before she was taken away to Arcadia, or as the person she would have aged to become. This means, among other things, that a changeling\u2019s mortal friends and relations are likely to recognize her when they see her again. Once again, though, since the Mask conforms to the changeling, recognition is less likely if the Lost underwent physiological changes apart from acquiring a seeming in Faerie. For example, the Mask of a Dancer taken when she was 10 and returned when she was 18 looks like an 18-year-old version of her pre-abduction self, while a Gristlegrinder who gained 50 pounds looks like his former self after going on an all-cheeseburger diet.</div> </div> </div> </div>Per 2e: <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL 2e Core, p214, Bargains - Benefits</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">This protection extends beyond the Mask \u2014 all changelings have some degree of concealment, but <u>the magic that makes human beings see them without their fae features</u> only extends so far.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>CtL 2e Core, p118, Manymask Merit</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">A changeling is usually stuck with the same Mask he left the Hedge with, an immutable combination of <u>remembered human traits.</u></div> </div> </div> </div>The Mask of a fae entity <i>can</i> differ substantially from its mien, but for most changelings who don't have a specific ability to mess with it their Mask is what their old mundane self would look like subjected to mundane physiological changes they underwent like aging and addition or subtraction of flesh, hair, and bone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2022-03-06T08:17:35-08:00","id":1475898,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#FF0000\"><b>Uhm, basically, this thread has received a lot of complaints. Well intentioned or accidental or not, this is really something that should be headed back to the drawing board, OP.<br /> <br /> I don't think the responses are going to get better either.</b></span><br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Author of <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Cthulhu-Armageddon-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01KUOM7SI/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982844&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Cthulhu+Armageddon\" target=\"_blank\">Cthulhu Armageddon</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Teenage-Weredeer-Bright-Falls-Mysteries-ebook/dp/B075TTN2FN/ref=sr_1_2?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982717&amp;sr=1-2&amp;keywords=Weredeer#customerReviews\" target=\"_blank\">I was a Teenage Weredeer</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Straight-Outta-Fangton-Comedic-Vampire-ebook/dp/B01KNHICCC/ref=sr_1_1?s=digital-text&amp;ie=UTF8&amp;qid=1535982774&amp;sr=1-1&amp;keywords=Straight+Outta+Fangton\" target=\"_blank\">Straight Outta Fangton</a></i>, <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Lucifers-Star-C-T-Phipps-ebook/dp/B01MDM9MCT/ref=mt_kindle?_encoding=UTF8&amp;me=&amp;qid=\" target=\"_blank\">Lucifer's Star</a>, </i>and the <i><a href=\"https://www.amazon.com/Rules-Supervillainy-Saga-Book-ebook/dp/B07MB89S33/\" target=\"_blank\">Supervillainy Saga</a>.</i><br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\"><b>Forum Terms of Use</b></a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/contact-us\" target=\"_blank\">the Contact Us link</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12002-ctphipps","name":"CTPhipps","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12002_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"13933"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}